  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds a 15-box pyramid (rows of 5, 4, 3, 2, 1) on a static floor, plus a heavy ball. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it or build it, so the physics, the shadows and the camera framing are untested. All bodies are real Aura3D physics bodies. The code calls `app.physics.step` itself, using a fixed 1/60 s step. Node bindings write the poses back to the meshes. The scene uses the `outdoor-day` look for lighting and shadows. The camera is a fixed perspective view from the side, aimed at the pyramid and the ball's path.\n\nThe ball sits about 9 m in front of the pyramid and is launched at it 1.5 s after load. Space rebuilds the scene with `app.setScene` and relaunches the ball immediately. I chose that because `AuraBodyHandle` has no way to reset a body's rotation, so a toppled box can't be put back any other way. The code sets `window.__EVAL_READY__` after `app.ready()` resolves and two animation frames have passed.\n\nI used `.then` instead of top-level `await`, because the project has no `vite.config.ts` and the default build target may reject top-level await.",
